`var` is function-scoped, so all three callbacks close over the same single `i`. The `setTimeout` callbacks run only after the loop finishes, when `i` is 3.

Fix: use `let`, which creates a fresh binding per iteration.

```js
for (let i = 0; i < 3; i++) {
  setTimeout(() => console.log(i), 0);
}
```
